Overlay patch 0024 (rev3: +audio-thread QoS): THE sibling-wide fuzzy-audio fix (device feedback
2026-07-19: every port except SoH crackles while the left thumb presses the
touch stick). Root cause: this port's OTRAudio_Thread produces audio ONLY on
the game loop's per-tick cv notify; on iOS the game loop IS the UIKit main
thread, so a pressed thumb's touch-event bursts delay the notify past the
ring's headroom -> underrun crackle. SoH upstream already evolved the loop
(5 ms self-pump + producer guard + pre-buffer reservoir, their clicks fix
#6594) which is why SoH alone is clean — the shells are byte-identical and
already coalesce axis sends AND redraws, so the shell is NOT the cause.
Ported SoH's loop shape with 2S2H's processing/cv_from_thread handshake
preserved (the main thread still waits for processing==false each tick);
notify only answers real gfx wakes. Tracks min buffered samples into an
atomic the 0008 rev5 probe reports as aud_min (0 = underrun; the retest
instrument). __IOS__-gated: the macOS build keeps pristine upstream
behavior. Coupled to 0008 rev5 (probe reads the atomic) — the series
applies atomically. Prescription for Starship/SpaghettiKart/Ghostship in
docs/PORTING-DELTAS.md: check your OTRAudio_Thread for the plain-wait loop.

